      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Aside from being demotivating when you see all the instances are above the recommended capacity (soft-cap), what use would this serve?\n\nJust look at the numbers for how many people are using your world, instead of counting instances. That should work better as a motivating factor anyway.\n\nWorld creators should not be treated differently just because they happened to be the ones that uploaded the world. If something like this is changes, it will just end up with confused players or bug reports from people that don't understand that some players see things differently.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
